<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="091" project="spaarke-modal-system">
  <metadata>
    <title>P7 — Retire solution-local navigation.ts copies (LegalWorkspace ≡ SmartTodo) — FR-18</title>
    <phase>7 OOB consolidation</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 090</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modify-then-delete of duplicated helper files with a clear consuming pattern (the shared hub from task 090); bounded blast radius (two solutions), no new architecture.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical dedup + caller repoint against an already-built hub; fully specified once 090 lands.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P7</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>090</deps>
    <tags>react, typescript, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>`src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/utils/navigation.ts` and `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/utils/navigation.ts` are byte-identical (both open at 80%×80% via `navigateTo` `target:2`). Retire BOTH by routing their callers through the shared `xrmNavigationServiceAdapter` at the OOB size scale (task 090 constants), then DELETE the two duplicate files. The 80%→85%(record)/70-80%(create-form) size collapse is acceptable pending the one-time P7 visual review (FR-18).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in TypeScript module retirement, Dataverse `navigateTo`, and cross-solution refactors. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Both `navigation.ts` copies are deleted; every caller in LegalWorkspace and SmartTodo routes through the shared `xrmNavigationServiceAdapter` at the OOB size scale from task 090; both solutions build green under `@types/react` 18 and React 19 with no dangling imports.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Discovery (project CLAUDE.md, 2026-08-01) confirmed `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/utils/navigation.ts` and `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/utils/navigation.ts` are byte-identical (both 4225 bytes) and both open at 80%×80% via `navigateTo target:2`. Spec FR-18 mandates retiring solution-local `navigation.ts` copies and routing all `navigateTo` through the two sanctioned hubs. Task 090 built the OOB size constants + hub consumption; this task repoints the callers of the two duplicate files to the shared adapter and deletes the duplicates. The size collapse from 80% to the named `record`/`create-form` sizes is a known, accepted change pending the one-time P7 visual review (spec "remaining assumption").</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="delete">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/utils/navigation.ts</file>
      <file role="delete">src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/utils/navigation.ts</file>
      <file role="reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/adapters/xrmNavigationServiceAdapter.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">callers of both `navigation.ts` copies in `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/**` and `src/solutions/SmartTodo/**`</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="090" status="pending">OOB size constants + the two hubs consuming them; the size scale the callers repoint onto.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Callers route through the single shared `@spaarke/ui-components` `xrmNavigationServiceAdapter`; MUST NOT reintroduce a solution-local navigation helper (CLAUDE.md §11 — one source of truth).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The 80%→85%(record)/70-80%(create-form) collapse is acceptable pending the one-time P7 visual review; MUST NOT silently preserve a bespoke 80% by pinning a per-caller size — surface any genuine 80% need for the review instead.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Keep OOB `navigateTo` for full main-form editing; only the launch size/route changes (NFR-05, client-only). MUST compile clean under `@types/react` 18 and React 19 (NFR-04).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Retiring duplicated solution-local navigation helpers onto the shared OOB hub</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/record-modal-selection.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="record-modal-selection" location=".claude/patterns/ui/record-modal-selection.md">OOB `navigateTo` record open at the 85%×85% invariant.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load both `navigation.ts` copies + the shared `xrmNavigationServiceAdapter`. Declare RIGOR: STANDARD.</step>
    <step order="1">Grep both solutions for imports/callers of the local `navigation.ts` (LegalWorkspace + SmartTodo); enumerate every call site.</step>
    <step order="2">Repoint each caller to the shared `xrmNavigationServiceAdapter` using the OOB named size (record/create-form) from task 090; map the former 80%×80% opens onto the appropriate named size.</step>
    <step order="3">Delete both `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/utils/navigation.ts` and `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/utils/navigation.ts`; grep to confirm zero remaining imports of either file.</step>
    <step order="4">Build both solutions and confirm green; confirm dual-React clean (`@types/react` 18 and React 19).</step>
    <step order="5">Note in `projects/spaarke-modal-system/notes/` any caller flagged as genuinely needing 80% for the one-time P7 visual review.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 091 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/spaarke-modal-system/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a specific caller genuinely needs the former 80% size (not the named `record`/`create-form` scale), note it for the one-time P7 visual review per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than forcing it to 85% silently or re-pinning a bespoke 80%.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Callers open at the standard OOB size (manual)">
      <steps>
        <step>Trigger a former `navigation.ts` open path in LegalWorkspace and in SmartTodo.</step>
        <step>Measure the opened modal against its viewport.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each opens at the named OOB size (record 85%×85% or create-form 70%×80%) via the shared hub; no site opens the old 80%×80% ad-hoc size.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark-mode note">
      <steps>
        <step>Observe the opened OOB modal under a dark host theme.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Dark-mode chrome is N/A here — the OOB `navigateTo` dialog chrome is host-owned, not a Spaarke component; only the launch size/route changed.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test LegalWorkspace and SmartTodo solutions</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/** callers repointed to the shared hub</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SmartTodo/** callers repointed to the shared hub</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Both `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/utils/navigation.ts` and `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/utils/navigation.ts` are deleted; a grep finds no remaining imports of either file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every former caller routes through the shared `xrmNavigationServiceAdapter` at an OOB named size from task 090.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both solutions build green under `@types/react` 18 and React 19 with no dangling imports.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Any caller genuinely needing the old 80% size is recorded for the P7 visual review rather than silently forced to 85%.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Modify-then-delete — no `&lt;justification&gt;` (retires duplicated existing files onto the shared hub; net component count decreases per NFR-06). Depends on 090 (constants + hubs). Runs in parallel group P7 with 092. The 80%→85/70-80 collapse is a spec-acknowledged accepted change pending the one-time P7 visual review.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all files in knowledge/files first. Follow task-execute.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
